        "prefix_token_count": 49,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Identify the given lengths and shapes.\n- Quadrilateral \\(CDEG\\) is a square with side length \\(CD = 3\\).\n- Quadrilateral \\(BEFH\\) is a rectangle with \\(BE = 5\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 458,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 460,
        "char_start": 171,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 149,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 150,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Determine the coordinates of points based on the given information.\n- Place point \\(C\\) at the origin \\((0,0)\\).\n- Point \\(D\\) will be at \\((3,0)\\) since \\(CD = 3\\).\n- Point \\(E\\) will be at \\((6,3)\\) because \\(CDEG\\) is a square and \\(CD = 3\\).\n- Point \\(G\\) will be at \\((3,3)\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 760,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 762,
        "char_start": 462,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 246,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 247,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Use the properties of the rectangle to find the coordinates of \\(B\\) and \\(H\\).\n- Since \\(BE = 5\\) and \\(E\\) is at \\((6,3)\\), point \\(B\\) must be at \\((1,3)\\) because the vertical distance from \\(B\\) to \\(E\\) is 3 (same as the side of the square) and the horizontal distance is \\(5 - 3 = 2\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1183,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1185,
        "char_start": 764,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 385,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 386,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Find the coordinates of \\(H\\).\n- Since \\(H\\) lies on both the line through \\(B\\) and the line through \\(E\\) extended, we need to find the intersection of these lines with the line \\(AG\\).\n- The line through \\(B\\) and \\(E\\) has a slope of \\(\\frac{3-3}{6-1} = 0\\), meaning it is a horizontal line at \\(y = 3\\).\n- The line through \\(A\\) and \\(G\\) has a slope of \\(\\frac{3-0}{3-0} = 1\\), so its equation is \\(y = x\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1746,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1748,
        "char_start": 1187,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 556,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 557,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: Solve for the intersection of \\(y = 3\\) and \\(y = x\\).\n- Setting \\(x = 3\\) gives us the point \\((3,3)\\), but this is point \\(G\\). We need to extend the line \\(AG\\) beyond \\(G\\).\n- The correct approach is to use the fact that \\(H\\) is directly above \\(B\\) vertically, maintaining the same y-coordinate as \\(B\\) but extending horizontally to intersect the line \\(AG\\).\n- Since \\(H\\) is directly above \\(B\\) and the line \\(AG\\) is \\(y = x\\), \\(H\\) must be at \\((3,3)\\) extended horizontally to intersect \\(AG\\), which means \\(H\\) is at \\((3+2,3) = (5,3)\\)."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1916,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1918,
        "char_start": 1750,
        "effective_step": 6,
        "end_token_index": 615,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 616,
        "step_number": 6,
        "text": "Step 6: Calculate the length \\(BH\\).\n- The length \\(BH\\) is the horizontal distance between \\(B\\) at \\((1,3)\\) and \\(H\\) at \\((5,3)\\).\n- This distance is \\(5 - 1 = 4\\)."
