  "raw_text": "Step 1: Identify the given lengths and shapes.\n- Quadrilateral \\(CDEG\\) is a square with side length \\(CD = 3\\).\n- Quadrilateral \\(BEFH\\) is a rectangle with \\(BE = 5\\).\n\nStep 2: Determine the coordinates of points based on the given information.\n- Place point \\(C\\) at the origin \\((0,0)\\).\n- Point \\(D\\) will be at \\((3,0)\\) since \\(CD = 3\\).\n- Point \\(E\\) will be at \\((6,3)\\) because \\(CDEG\\) is a square and \\(CD = 3\\).\n- Point \\(G\\) will be at \\((3,3)\\).\n\nStep 3: Use the properties of the rectangle to find the coordinates of \\(B\\) and \\(H\\).\n- Since \\(BE = 5\\) and \\(E\\) is at \\((6,3)\\), point \\(B\\) must be at \\((1,3)\\) because the vertical distance from \\(B\\) to \\(E\\) is 3 (same as the side of the square) and the horizontal distance is \\(5 - 3 = 2\\).\n\nStep 4: Find the coordinates of \\(H\\).\n- Since \\(H\\) lies on both the line through \\(B\\) and the line through \\(E\\) extended, we need to find the intersection of these lines with the line \\(AG\\).\n- The line through \\(B\\) and \\(E\\) has a slope of \\(\\frac{3-3}{6-1} = 0\\), meaning it is a horizontal line at \\(y = 3\\).\n- The line through \\(A\\) and \\(G\\) has a slope of \\(\\frac{3-0}{3-0} = 1\\), so its equation is \\(y = x\\).\n\nStep 5: Solve for the intersection of \\(y = 3\\) and \\(y = x\\).\n- Setting \\(x = 3\\) gives us the point \\((3,3)\\), but this is point \\(G\\). We need to extend the line \\(AG\\) beyond \\(G\\).\n- The correct approach is to use the fact that \\(H\\) is directly above \\(B\\) vertically, maintaining the same y-coordinate as \\(B\\) but extending horizontally to intersect the line \\(AG\\).\n- Since \\(H\\) is directly above \\(B\\) and the line \\(AG\\) is \\(y = x\\), \\(H\\) must be at \\((3,3)\\) extended horizontally to intersect \\(AG\\), which means \\(H\\) is at \\((3+2,3) = (5,3)\\).\n\nStep 6: Calculate the length \\(BH\\).\n- The length \\(BH\\) is the horizontal distance between \\(B\\) at \\((1,3)\\) and \\(H\\) at \\((5,3)\\).\n- This distance is \\(5 - 1 = 4\\).\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{4}<|im_end|>",
